  "method": [
    "The three invoked runs used (version 1)(allow default). An exec of /bin/sh wrote its parent PID to a private marker. The worker then performed read_fresh on a private FIFO, a plain file/create, and read_fresh on a second FIFO. The create_then_unlink plan finally unlinked the target. No other process wrote to the target.",
    "The caller connected a writer to the first FIFO and withheld the byte until after CLI return and lstat. The repo footprint observer checked the worker path and PID/start time before and after registering EVFILT_PROC NOTE_EXIT, and checked the same generation at CLI return. The exit watch had no event at either of the two holds.",
    "After releasing the first read the caller connected to the second FIFO, sampled the target, released the second read, observed the registered exit, and sampled again. ENOENT below is a caller lstat result. No worker errno was available in the timeout envelope.",
    "The retry used the same saved specimen bytes with a longer client deadline and both FIFO reads released promptly. For missing_parent the caller created the missing parent directory before retrying. For create_only a caller descriptor on the existing target remained open across the retry and its device/inode matched the path afterward.",
    "The separate short-timeout case used only a single plain create on an initially absent name. The two-terminal recipe used create, read_fresh on a FIFO, then unlink."
